14. Create RBD pool
An RBD pool in Ceph is a storage pool used for RADOS Block Device (RBD) images.
RBD provides block storage similar to a virtual disk/LUN, which can be used by:

Think of it like this:

Ceph Cluster
 └── Pool (rbd pool)
      └── RBD Images (virtual disks)

# ceph osd lspools
1 .mgr

# ceph osd pool create vm-pool 32
pool 'vm-pool' created

# ceph osd lspools
1 .mgr
2 vm-pool

- Enable RBD Application on Pool
# ceph osd pool application enable  vm-pool rbd
enabled application 'rbd' on pool 'vm-pool'

Verify:
# ceph osd pool application get  vm-pool
{
    "rbd": {}
}

- Set Replication Size
# ceph osd pool set vm-pool size 3
set pool 2 size to 3

# ceph osd pool set vm-pool min_size 2
set pool 2 min_size to 2

Verify:
# ceph osd pool get vm-pool size
size: 3

# ceph osd pool get vm-pool min_size
min_size: 2
